innova2_shell_examples -- examples for the Innova-2 (Mellanox/NVIDIA Innova-2 Flex, Xilinx XCKU15P + ConnectX-5)
running the inn2x r10 shell. Copyright 2026 the innova2 contributors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(LICENSE), except as noted below. REUSE.toml and the SPDX headers give the licence of every file; LICENSE_AUDIT.md
lists every file with its provenance.

Third-party material in this repository:

* fld_lite/e5/zuc/rtl, rtl4 and the files annotated so: the ZUC AFU from FlexDriver's flexdriver-zuc,
  Copyright (c) 2020-2021 Gabi Malka, BSD-2-Clause (fld_lite/e5/zuc/LICENSE.flexdriver-zuc).

* fld_lite/s0/prm.h, fld_lite/e1/prm.h: the MLX5_* accessor macros follow include/linux/mlx5/device.h, Copyright
  Mellanox Technologies Ltd., dual GPL-2.0 / OpenIB.org BSD; used under the OpenIB.org BSD licence
  (LICENSES/Linux-OpenIB.txt). mlx5_ifc.h itself is copied from the installed OFED tree at build time, not included.
  Three CQ field positions that OFED's mlx5_ifc.h leaves `reserved` (fld_lite/e2, e3) are taken from DPDK's
  drivers/common/mlx5/mlx5_prm.h (BSD-3-Clause, 6WIND S.A. / Mellanox Technologies): facts, no code copied.

* fld_lite/innova2_peermem, fld_lite/hostmem/innova2_hostmem.c: our Linux kernel modules, GPL-2.0-only
  (LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt).

* examples/memcached/kernels/pipeline_orig2015 (as published) and examples/memcached/kernels/pipeline (modified where
  marked "innova2:"): the memcached pipeline from Xilinx HLx_Examples (github.com/Xilinx/HLx_Examples,
  Acceleration/memcached), Copyright (c) 2016, Xilinx, Inc., BSD-3-Clause (LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt). Modifications:
  globals.h testbench slot size 1024 -> 2048; valueStore.cpp / flashValueStore.cpp remux no longer falls through from
  IDLE into OPCODECHECK in one cycle (timing); hashTable/memWrite.cpp: a SET that overwrites a key whose bucket has no
  free bin no longer hangs the pipeline.

* examples/hls4ml/kernel/firmware: generated by hls4ml (github.com/fastmachinelearning/hls4ml, Apache-2.0);
  nnet_utils/ are hls4ml's templates. The weights come from our model trained on the dataset below.

* examples/hls4ml/jets.bin: derived from the hls4ml_lhc_jets_hlf dataset by Maurizio Pierini, Javier Duarte, Nhan Tran,
  Marat Freytsis and Vladimir Loncar (doi:10.5281/zenodo.3602260, OpenML 42468), CC-BY-4.0. Changes: the test split
  only, standardised and quantised to ap_fixed<16,6>, with hls4ml's emulated outputs appended (model/make_jets.py).

* examples/vitislibs/overlay: benchmark directories from AMD Vitis Libraries (github.com/Xilinx/Vitis_Libraries,
  Apache-2.0, Copyright Xilinx, Inc. / Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.). Files we changed say so in their headers or in the
  directory's README.md; the others are unmodified copies.
  - security/L1/benchmarks/aes256CbcDecrypt_4pu: the kernel and host of tag v2020.2_rel, the build files of
    v2023.2_update1;
  - codec/L2/demos/jpegDec_fix: jpegDec of v2023.2_update1; kernel/XAcc_idct.hpp changed (copyInfo writes);
  - data_compression/L2/demos/zstd_decompress_fix: zstd_decompress of v2023.2_update1; kernel/zstd_decompress.hpp
    (two decoder bugs) and kernel/zstd_decompress_stream.cpp (history size) changed;
  - data_compression/L2/demos/snappy_streaming_fix: snappy_streaming of v2023.2_update1;
    kernel/snappy_decompress_details.hpp changed (chunk-header loop);
  - solver/L2/benchmarks/gtsv_1024: gtsv of v2023.2_update1; kernel_gtsv.cpp set to AMD's published size.

* examples/compression/patches, examples/vitislibs/host_patches: our patches to AMD Vitis Libraries files (Apache-2.0);
  their context lines are AMD's. examples/vitislibs/graphdata/tools/lp_csim.cpp contains AMD Vitis Libraries graph
  kernel code (Apache-2.0); sssp_csim.cpp and tc_csim.cpp include AMD's headers from a Vitis Libraries checkout.

Fetched at build or run time, not included: AMD Vitis Libraries v2023.2_update1 (Apache-2.0; examples/compression
applies the patches in examples/compression/patches, examples/vitislibs builds its benchmarks); AMD Vitis_Accel_Examples
(MIT; examples/suite); the SuiteSparse Matrix Collection graphs (CC-BY-4.0; examples/vitislibs/graphdata/prepare.sh);
the hls4ml_lhc_jets_hlf dataset (CC-BY-4.0; examples/hls4ml/model).

The xclbins in xclbin/ contain, besides our kernels, the AMD IP of the platform's dynamic region (LicenseRef-AMD-IP:
AMD's terms allow these cores to be distributed as a bitstream, to program AMD devices only). Further: zuc.xclbin the
BSD-2-Clause ZUC AFU and memcached.xclbin the BSD-3-Clause memcached pipeline -- binaries built from them must
reproduce the copyright notice, conditions and disclaimer above (LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt, LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt),
and Xilinx's name may not be used to endorse or promote products derived from the memcached pipeline; the compression
xclbins Apache-2.0 code from Vitis Libraries; hls4ml.xclbin Apache-2.0 code generated by hls4ml.
